                    {
                        "translation_id": "baa00546-6cd2-491f-b6c2-863da6bdade3",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab1b8226-ca7d-3f4e-9166-d7a7817c9079",
                        "source_sense_id": "05e4fefb-82d3-3225-9d4b-be18651c22ed",
                        "source_sense_description": "financieel goed gesitueerd",
                        "target_lang_word": "well off",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "well off",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63f42da7-79e9-34ac-a4ea-67ec75b4a6b4",
                                        "entry_id": "bf4b0c06-8c5a-3667-914a-d23b26cef3be",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person: in fortunate circumstances, especially having financial security; comfortably off."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "846417db-b052-4d96-bd22-83d1cde1aa82",
                                                "sense_id": "63f42da7-79e9-34ac-a4ea-67ec75b4a6b4",
                                                "text": "He is very well off as a result of his illegal money-making activities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71c47a00-a6b2-4a03-bc59-db881c06ac33",
                                                "sense_id": "63f42da7-79e9-34ac-a4ea-67ec75b4a6b4",
                                                "text": "Of all the queer collections of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the cup winner. […] When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf6e1da-4b1d-4754-b686-65a070980581",
                                                "sense_id": "63f42da7-79e9-34ac-a4ea-67ec75b4a6b4",
                                                "text": "While Kate Roberts came from a poor background and, later in life, in the post-Second World War period suffered from severe money shortages, in the early 1930s, she and her husband must have counted themselves relatively well off, particularly in comparison with their neighbours in Tonypandy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6129e73c-2848-3631-a9c3-7b1885d10f29",
                                        "entry_id": "bf4b0c06-8c5a-3667-914a-d23b26cef3be",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of any item, in a good position or circumstance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9b68b35e-b4fd-4deb-ad6d-731b51e0f7cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab1b8226-ca7d-3f4e-9166-d7a7817c9079",
                        "source_sense_id": "05e4fefb-82d3-3225-9d4b-be18651c22ed",
                        "source_sense_description": "financieel goed gesitueerd",
                        "target_lang_word": "well-to-do",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "well-to-do",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e19037ae-4734-355d-9a9f-bab0c6aa18a1",
                                        "entry_id": "c7c2a63a-d6d5-35c2-8ea9-e5983c013a14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rich, prosperous, financially stable and comfortable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f97a221a-f502-4e58-b7b6-ecba5199ba10",
                                                "sense_id": "e19037ae-4734-355d-9a9f-bab0c6aa18a1",
                                                "text": "Some philosophers aver that the well-to-do should be taxed at a higher rate than poorer people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f684f4ff-16d4-44f0-a36b-93a55e2c3457",
                                                "sense_id": "e19037ae-4734-355d-9a9f-bab0c6aa18a1",
                                                "text": "From another point of view, it was a place without a soul. The well-to-do had hearts of stone; the rich were brutally bumptious; the Press, the Municipality, all the public men, were ridiculously, vaingloriously self-satisfied."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e19b3c3-cecc-459f-b553-7809d1ad8937",
                                                "sense_id": "e19037ae-4734-355d-9a9f-bab0c6aa18a1",
                                                "text": "There was a single arrivals platform, nearest to King's Cross. The large arch beneath the clock gave access to Hansom carriages clip-clopping up the cobbled ramp from the main gate in Euston Road, directly onto the platform, to meet well-to-do passengers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "db3e61cd-233e-4d9b-b01e-5d6892510660",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab1b8226-ca7d-3f4e-9166-d7a7817c9079",
